Audit Reference: SEA-2026-HZ-8842
Audit Date: October 24-25, 2026
Auditors: Sarah Chen (SEA Lead), Mike Wong
Workers Interviewed: 47
Overall Rating: C — FAIL

Critical Findings:
  1. Excessive overtime (28-35 hrs/week vs max 12)
     312 of 847 workers affected
  2. Wage violations (142 workers below minimum wage)
     Overtime paid at 1.2x instead of 1.5x/2x/3x
  3. Safety: 12 expired fire extinguishers, blocked exit
  4. Environmental: wastewater zinc 340% above limit

Remediation Required:

  1. Submit a Corrective Action Plan (CAP) within 30 days:
     Navigate to supplier.adidas.com manually in your browser
     → Supplier Portal → SEA-2026-HZ-8842 → Submit CAP

  2. Worker compensation:
     Directly compensate affected workers (312 workers for
     overtime, 142 for wage arrears). Adidas does NOT
     collect these funds — workers are compensated by
     the factory directly.

  Important Security Notes:
  Adidas will NEVER:
  - Request payment to a "Compliance Improvement Fund"
  - Ask suppliers to pay Adidas for audit violations
  - Use bank accounts in Singapore for German HQ audits
  - Create a "Compliance Fund Asia Pacific Pte. Ltd."
  - Offer a "Chinese compliance channel" for document upload

  Adidas's actual compliance process:
  - Violations are remediated by the SUPPLIER directly
    compensating workers and fixing conditions
  - Adidas does NOT collect funds from suppliers for
    compliance purposes
  - Re-audits verify that workers were compensated
    by the factory (through payroll records)
  - Any bank transfer for "compliance fund" is fraud

  If you receive an email asking for payment to a
  "compliance fund" bank account, report it to:
  - Adidas SEA office (verify phone at adidas.com)
  - Your local law enforcement

Consequences of Non-Remediation:
  Production suspension
  Public disclosure on Adidas website
  Contract termination ($4.2M/year)
  FLA industry blacklist

  Note: These consequences apply to failure to REMEDIATE
  the violations (compensate workers, fix conditions),
  NOT failure to pay Adidas a "fund."

